Open Vanilla / Open Vanilla 0022 — the login/download queue: a busy realm puts players in line instead of falling over.

* New src/queue.rs: two gates, in memory, both off unless QUEUE_ENABLED=1.
  - Download gate (first-time players only): at most QUEUE_DOWNLOADS fetch the game data at once.
    The data routes (/data/* and the .wasm bundle) need the account's data grant, given when the
    line lets the player through. A returning player — the page keeps the marker the realm sealed
    (ChaCha20-Poly1305, master key) when their first download finished, naming the account and the
    data version, and the wasm is still in the HTTP cache — skips this gate.
  - World gate (everyone): at most QUEUE_WORLD players in the world or signing in, counted as
    admitted tickets that keep polling (the page heartbeats every 30 s). /api/play (the game
    sign-in) needs this browser's world pass (X-Queue-Pass). CMaNGOS PlayerLimit stays above it.
  - Fair FIFO across both gates (by join time), one ticket per browser (session cookie), a cap on
    waiting tickets per IP, admissions paced by a token bucket, tickets dropped (with their slot)
    when not polled for 3 minutes, a download slot given back after 15 minutes at most.
* Endpoints: POST /api/queue/join {marker?} → ticket, position, waiting, eta_secs, gate (or "go");
  GET /api/queue/status?ticket= → the same, "go" carries the world pass; POST /api/queue/done
  {ticket} (download finished: frees the slot, returns the marker); POST /api/queue/leave {ticket}.
* The play page (templates/play.html): the queue window from docs/queue/queue-window.html — "You're
  in line", place, "of N waiting", progress bar, ETA, "Keep this tab open", the realm busy
  indicator, Cancel, and "No wait in your own world: Play Solo in the free desktop app" — before
  any download starts, and again between download and sign-in if the world is full; phone portrait
  and landscape layouts. Art and fonts in assets/queue/, served at /brand/queue/*; the backdrop and
  logo are the realm's own /brand files. The marker lives in localStorage "ov-data".
* web/boot.js: optional opts.beforeInit(ui) hook between the download and init() (the queue uses
  it to report the download done, wait for the world and only then fetch the credentials).
* With the queue off, nothing changes: the endpoints answer 404, nothing is checked, and the page
  runs the same sequence as before (the credential fetch is now a signIn() function).
* tests/queue.rs: queue off = no change; FIFO; download slots free up; expiry; per-IP cap;
  returning-player bypass and marker checks; world gate blocks sign-in beyond QUEUE_WORLD; pacing;
  env parsing. The other harnesses gain `queue: Default::default()`.

Env vars: QUEUE_ENABLED (0), QUEUE_DOWNLOADS (25), QUEUE_WORLD (120), QUEUE_PER_IP (4),
QUEUE_ADMIT_PER_MIN (60, per gate), QUEUE_ADMIT_BURST (10), QUEUE_DATA_VERSION (unset: derived from
the wasm bundle's size/mtime and boot-manifest.json in REALM_WWW; set it to a build id to control
when returning players must download again).

